---
// Shown by nginx for any address that doesn't exist (error_page in nginx.conf)
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout pageTitle="404: Page not found">
  <h1>404: There's Nothing Here!</h1>
  <p>
    You have encountered a 404 error. That means that you went to an address at
    Loathers.net that doesn't actually have any content. But those with hungry
    eyes and a pleasant heart might still read things, if you dare to do so. Try
    checking out:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/">The home page</a>, for our newest posts</li>
    <li>
      <a href="/analysis">Analysis</a>, for IOTM reviews and strategy guides
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/scripting">Scripting</a>, for guides to writing KoL scripts
    </li>
    <li><a href="/tools">Tools</a>, for the Loathers web tools</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    As a small easter egg, though, I am going to list out a handful of things
    related to the number 404 in subjects germane to this website. This is a
    classic Captain Scotch move, writing things that absolutely nobody in the
    world will ever read.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      The 404th item in the Kingdom of Loathing is the <a
        href="https://wiki.kingdomofloathing.com/Acoustic_guitarrr"
        >acoustic guitarrr</a
      >; the 404th song to chart at #1 on the U.S. Billboard Hot 100 was "Play
      That Funky Music" by Wild Cherry, which does indeed feature a funky
      guitarrr... it's electric, though. Darn the 70s!
    </li>
    <li>
      The 404th monster in KoL is the <a
        href="https://wiki.kingdomofloathing.com/Floating_platter_of_hors_d%27oeuvres"
        >floating platter of hors d'oeuvres</a
      >. The 404th recipe in Mrs. Beeton's <a
        href="https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/10136"
        >Book of Household Management</a
      > is the "Custard Sauce for Sweet Puddings or Tarts". This is hardly an hors
      d'oeuvre, but could certainly be served on a haunted floating platter.
    </li>
    <li>
      The 404th effect in KoL is <a
        href="https://wiki.kingdomofloathing.com/Braaains">Braaains</a
      >... beaten out ever-so-slightly in value by the <i>totally distinct</i> effect
      #405,
      <a href="https://wiki.kingdomofloathing.com/Braaaaaains">Braaaaaains</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      At exactly 404 mainstat in KoL, you reach level 21. Some say that is the
      most missing level of all. Not me, though.
    </li>
    <li>
      <a
        href="https://github.com/loathers/garbage-collector/commit/ebdf9753ab621c6562b62ffe9321aa2a053f8b84"
        >The 404th commit in garbage-collector</a
      > featured a refactor of class chocolate logic; a 404 by any other sweet could
      taste so... sweet? I don't really know what I'm doing with this bit.
    </li>
    <li>
      <a
        href="https://github.com/loathers/autoscend/commit/220b9d39388f6d9c0328be5ecb0c91d18c874eac"
        >The 404th commit in autoscend</a
      > featured a fix to Blech House in softcore way back in 2019, when Blech House
      was introduced. Blech, we've got a 404 in the House! (It's good that nobody's
      reading this, or else I would be instantly arrested.)
    </li>
  </ul>
</BaseLayout>
